# Every environment variable the project reads (REL-2).
# Copy to .env and fill in. Never commit .env.
#
# You only need the keys for the providers your config actually uses.
# Config holds no secrets (CFG-2); providers read them from here.

# --- Core ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Signs Confirm and Cancel button payloads (CONF-3). Any long random string.
OPENBOX_SECRET=

# --- Database -----------------------------------------------------------
# The Supabase project the agent runs against, with the service role key.
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
# Direct Postgres connection, used by `openbox migrate` and the integration
# tests. Left empty, both fall back to the local stack that `bun run db:up`
# starts, which is postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:54322/postgres
#
# An agent on the pgvector retriever needs this at run time too, not only to
# migrate: it ranks with pgvector's distance operator, which PostgREST cannot
# express, so it opens a connection of its own. An agent on the default
# `local` retriever never does, and needs only the two Supabase values above.
DATABASE_URL=

# --- Brains -------------------------------------------------------------
# OpenRouter brain, and the OpenRouter transcriber, which is the one to
# reach for (DEP-2): its transcription endpoint serves 28 speech models on
# this one key. Also Jev on its OpenRouter route. One key, three uses.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# Claude Agent SDK brain.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OpenAI Agents SDK brain, the OpenAI Decisions decision model and the
# OpenAI embedder. There is no OpenAI transcriber: every OpenAI speech
# model is reachable on the OpenRouter key above, so a second adapter to
# the same models was not built (DEP-2).
OPENAI_API_KEY=
# The Claude Code CLI brain runs `claude --bare`, which reads
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY above and never a logged in session (BRAIN-1). The
# Codex CLI brain keeps its own login and uses OPENAI_API_KEY only when one
# is set. Both are for building and local testing only (BRAIN-4).

# --- Decision model -----------------------------------------------------
# Jev through the TypeSafe API. Jev through OpenRouter uses OPENROUTER_API_KEY.
# TypeSafe is in early access behind a waitlist, so the OpenRouter route is
# the one most agents can use today (docs/Known.md K8).
TYPESAFE_API_KEY=

# --- Transcribers -------------------------------------------------------
# Transcription defaults to OpenRouter, on the key above, with
# elevenlabs/scribe-v2 as the model. Nothing below is needed for that.
#
# Sarvam is the second transcriber and the only route to Saaras, which
# covers 22 Indian languages and code-mixed Hinglish that no model on
# OpenRouter is built for. It ships untested until there is real audio to
# test it with, so this key is only needed by an agent whose config names
# `sarvam`, or to settle whether the OpenRouter default handles Hinglish
# (docs/Known.md K21).
SARVAM_API_KEY=

# --- Running the live tests --------------------------------------------
# The core's own suite is offline by default. Set OPENBOX_LIVE=1 to also run
# the tests in packages/core/test/live, which call real providers and cost
# real money. They use the keys above.
OPENBOX_LIVE=
# Which model the live brain tests use. Defaults to a cheap one.
OPENBOX_LIVE_MODEL=
# The Codex live test needs its own switch as well as OPENBOX_LIVE. Codex
# runs on whatever login it has rather than a key, so there is no way to
# tell "not set up" from "broken" without running it.
OPENBOX_LIVE_CODEX=
